From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 05:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luma: frost and glass are one light material

Owner, 2026-09-18, on Shell .113: "FROST mode. dash is dark? and titlebars
are not frost, they're light. Same happens with glass." 0150, 0152 and 0157
had made frost and glass smoked veils carrying white ink on every Shell
surface, while application windows had just become light see-through panels
again. Together they read as a dark shelf under light windows, and neither
looked like the frosted panels the Appearance thumbnails show.

Frost and glass are now one light material everywhere: a light veil over the
blurred wallpaper carrying dark ink, the same material application windows
use. Frost is the denser, strongly blurred veil (radius 38, saturation 1.6);
glass lets clearly more wallpaper through, with less blur (radius 18,
saturation 1.35) and a brighter light rim.

  - SURFACE_INK: frost islands rgba(246,247,249,.80), menus and sheets .88,
    notification cards .88; glass islands rgba(250,250,251,.62), menus and
    sheets .80, cards .76. Ink is one step deeper than paper's (#1f262d and
    #394047 on frost, #161b20 and #1f242a on glass) because a veil over a
    black wallpaper is only mid grey; hover and press are dark washes; no
    text shadow on any mode. LIGHT_FAMILY names light, frost and glass.
  - Every stylesheet rule written for luma-surface-light now also names
    frost and glass, with the opaque light veils swapped for the translucent
    ones and paper's inks for the deeper ones; every frost/glass rule that
    carried smoked colours loses them and keeps its geometry. That covers
    the Shelf islands, the Well, the clock, Quick Options and its sheets
    (0164), notifications, the dock previews and tooltips, arrange mode
    (0167), the capture and sharing tools, the administrator prompt and
    Cast. Menus, the beam OSD and the prompt/share/capture cards take the
    veils explicitly, and the Well's recording amber is the ledger's deeper
    one. The notification Sass maps are regenerated from the new ledger.
  - The status cluster and the Well take the light recess and light ink on
    frost and glass (panel.js), and the Shell loads its light variant sheet
    for them (getStyleVariant), so overlays the variant sheet owns follow.
  - The filled-control state is a deeper slate (#4a5a6e frost, #3b4757
    glass) so an on toggle stands 3:1 from the veil over any wallpaper.
  - Menu section headings (PERSONALIZE, SYSTEM) were 11px text at 46% of
    the ink, 2.66:1 in light and 3.98:1 in dark; they are 72% and 62%,
    5.9:1 and 5.7:1, and the frost and glass headings take the ledger's.

Every text pair holds 4.5:1 and every glyph 3:1 composited over pure black,
mid grey, pure white and Luma's wallpapers blurred as the compositor blurs
them, with a recess and a pressed fill stacked on the veil:
tests/unit/lumaSurfaceInk.js gates the ledger (now including mid grey and a
light-family check), and data/theme/verify-treatment-ink.py fails the build
if near-white ink reaches a light-family surface or a control leaves its
ledger. Reduce Transparency and high contrast still resolve to opaque light.
